          "body": "## Scope\n\nCloses #353.\n\nPilot users/profiles and teams/memberships across both database engines, using idiomatic and matched-intent declarations. No package behavior changes.\n\nStart review at `research/schema_comparison/README.md`, then model declarations and raw SQL probes. Generated SQL, reflected structural diffs, and full observations are committed beside the runner.\n\n## Findings\n\n- All 128 shared-contract checks passed across eight runs.\n- Forty diagnostic observations expose SQLite STRICT and ID-reuse differences, plus MariaDB integer-range and collation differences.\n- Explicitly matched declarations agree on the measured behavior.\n- Python defaults did not become server defaults in either library.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran the experiment on SQLite 3.50.4 and temporary MariaDB 12.3.2 servers.\n- `uv run --group research snektest tests research/schema_comparison/test_experiment.py`: 1212 passed.\n- `uv run --group research ty check`: passed.\n- `uv run --group research ruff check .`: passed.\n- `uv run --group research ruff format --check .`: passed.\n- Bare snektest failed collection with `Empty module name`; explicit paths cover the package suite and research checks.\n\nDependencies are in an optional research group. Database versions are recorded, not provisioned by the runner. Broader type/default scenarios and MariaDB LTS coverage remain future research.\n",
